@openuidev/lang-core 0.2.18: a failed Query is not fetched again until its arguments change.

The query manager keeps a cache entry per Query and its arguments. A fetch that fails leaves the entry with no data,
so the next evaluateQueries (every state change and every re-render of the canvas) starts the same fetch again, and a
canvas whose Query fails loops on requests. The entry now records that it failed, and evaluateQueries fetches it again
only when the Query's cache key (its tool and arguments) changed; a manual refresh (invalidate, @Run(query)) still
fetches. The Java prototype hand-patched the same fix into its minified bundle (runtime commit 90960c4).
Reviewed Oct 22, 2026. Applied by libs/refresh.mjs to dist/index.mjs after the telemetry patch.

